## Current Learner/Course Status

Existing DB/schema and scripts already model course-related content: `course`, `course_enrollment`, `course_module`, `course_module_in_course`, `course_module_requires`, `course_module_review`, `module_completion`, `module_uses_artifact`, and `challenge`.

Learner Units 00-06 are complete or documented:

- Unit 00 documented the baseline: `/learn`, `/courses`, and `/challenges` are placeholder-level; dynamic learner route trees and learner component folders were not present.
- Unit 01 added course-scoped module completion and standalone module version auditing.
- Unit 02 added idempotent module/course XP awards.
- Unit 03 added the typed server-only learner data layer. Course-context completion remains separate from standalone completion, and `course_enrollment.progress` is treated as a derived cache.
- Unit 04 added published content immutability at both the database trigger layer and the vault upsert script layer.
- Units 05/06 added first-class learning assets, Supabase Storage-backed vault asset publishing, and `learning_asset` artifact links.

Current app routes `/learn`, `/courses`, and `/challenges` still exist but remain placeholder-level until UI route units land. Planned routes include `/modules`, `/modules/[moduleSlug]`, `/courses/[slug]`, `/courses/[courseSlug]/m/[moduleSlug]`, and `/challenges/[slug]`.

Remaining formal learner units are 07-15: shared learner components, learn hub/catalog routes, course detail/enrollment UI, module reader shell, quiz/completion actions, asset rendering/private URLs, read-only challenge detail, route polish/states, and integration/E2E coverage.
